    "title": "Victory Church hosts candlelight service in honor of Christmas Eve - NewsBreak",
    "text": "7 hours ago TULSA, Okla. — Churches across Green Country held services on Wednesday for Christmas Eve, including Victory Church.\nThe church held a candlelight service, which began at 6:30 p.m.\nThousands of people gathered to reflect on the story of Jesus, take communion, and worship on the night before Christmas.\n“I think we live in a world with terrorism and chaos and people need peace,” said Senior Pastor Paul Daughtery. “You won’t find it sitting under a tree or watching football. Ultimately, our peace is going to come through Jesus, and that's what Christmas is about.”\nIf you were unable to attend Wednesday’s service in person and are interested in watching it, you can do so below:\n2025 Victory Church XMAS Eve service",
